This function should merge overlapping intervals, but merge([[1, 4], [2, 3], [5, 7], [6, 8]]) returns [[1, 3], [5, 8]] instead of [[1, 4], [5, 8]]. Why, and how do I fix it?

```python
def merge(intervals):
    intervals.sort()
    merged = [intervals[0]]
    for start, end in intervals[1:]:
        last = merged[-1]
        if start <= last[1]:
            last[1] = end
        else:
            merged.append([start, end])
    return merged
```
